# finish/wear: T1's wear, mended never broken (STYLE_P2 27.3; P2C_CONTRACTS 3b W; LADDER-FINISH, ladder slice i3).
# A STAMP set (proposed `tags stamp`): laid once per connected W blob of a part's composed view, its origin on the blob's
# top-left; the view is picked by the blob: one row tall -> `hem` (repeated along the row from its left end: a notch every
# 6 px, the hem pixel dropped to the material's step 0 so the outline stays closed); else `<cloth|metal><w>x<h>` (w, h
# capped at 3; metal when most of the blob is Metal / Metal2 / Blade), cells off the blob skipped. Cells:
#   ~ (ink 1)  the patch: the piece's own material one step darker (i3: i2's leather-2 scrap matched the wooden shield
#              and the buff quilt read it as dirt; the linen stitch dots read as a pair of eyes on the shield)
#   ^ (ink 3)  the patch's lit top-left edge, one step lighter: at 3x a sewn / nailed-on piece, at 1x a darker inset
#   + linen 3  (spare) pale thread
#   $ leather 2 (spare)
#   % leather 1 tarnish: a warm rust-brown cluster, 2-3 px, only where the piece owner put W (the metal's shadow side)
#   = (ink 0)  the frayed hem's notch
# Proposed rules (LADDER-DOLL): in a stamp an ink cell keeps the slot and MOVES the step by (k - 2), clamped 0..4; a cell
# of any other slot writes slot and step absolutely; outlines (step 0) never change. Piece owners: one or two W blobs a
# piece, a patch 3x2 (2x2 shows a single stitch), wear 6 % of the piece at most (C12 d). `rest` is the periodic fallback.
use person
body adult
role overlay finish.wear
legend ~ ink 1
legend + linen 3
legend $ leather 2
legend % leather 1
legend = ink 0
legend ^ ink 3
tags tile overlay stamp
on-region W

view D key cloth2x2 origin 0 0
|^~
|~~

view D key cloth3x2 origin 0 0
|^^~
|~~~

view D key cloth2x3 origin 0 0
|^~
|~~
|~~

view D key cloth3x3 origin 0 0
|^^~
|~~~
|~~~

view D key metal2x2 origin 0 0
|.%
|%%

view D key metal3x2 origin 0 0
|.%.
|%%.

view D key metal2x3 origin 0 0
|.%
|%%
|..

view D key metal3x3 origin 0 0
|.%.
|%%.
|...

view D key hem origin 0 0
|.=....

view D key rest origin 0 0
|+~
|~~
